# Grbl on a mill. Written from Grbl's public G-code documentation
# (gnea/grbl, "Grbl v1.1 Commands"), no firmware source.
#
# G21 is mm, G90 absolute, G94 mm per minute (Grbl's feed). M3 turns the
# spindle on clockwise and M5 turns it off; S is the speed, written by
# the job. $H homes, when the machine has endstops; it is not in the
# start code, so a job can begin from the origin you set. $ settings
# stay in the controller.
family = cnc
dialect = grbl
send = file
features = spindle homing
start = G21 ; mm
start += G90 ; absolute
start += G94 ; mm per minute
start += M5 ; spindle off
end = M5
end += G0 Z5
end += G0 X0 Y0
